{"aah":{"id":"d12c4951-c5ae-42c8-917f-a269e72af531","word":"aah","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"expressing amazement or surprise","word":"nossa"}],"pos":"intj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Aah! That's amazing!","bold_text_offsets":[[0,4]],"type":"example","id":"4ea58ee9-ad2d-4377-812b-75e0b92eaeb3"},{"text":"'Aaah!' they sigh, as the silvery Space Shuttle races heavenwards on top of a towering pillar of flame.","ref":"1985, Joan Morrison, chapter 5, in Share House Blues, Boolarong Publications, page 62:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,5]],"id":"71187ac6-ec5d-4e7d-822c-a034acc47bd9"}],"links":[["amazement","amazement"],["surprise","surprise"],["enthusiasm","enthusiasm"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["Indication of amazement or surprise or enthusiasm."],"id":"77cb067a-c2d7-4b48-a2e5-f1597b96c852"},{"examples":[{"text":"Yet I remember—aah! how should I forget?","ref":"1834, Edgar Allan Poe, The Assignation:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[15,19]],"id":"0d22c1a2-d538-4c7b-ae4a-4d868dc08d56"}],"links":[["joy","joy"],["pleasure","pleasure"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["Indication of joyful pleasure."],"id":"e978a6d0-3882-46b6-b2b4-06230c809746"},{"examples":[{"text":"Aah, I feel so bad for you...","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"d0002ba0-1323-4b31-9af2-0acb983a4922"}],"glosses":["Indication of sympathy."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"bec981ea-5a15-409d-94f1-b1e88e72d6ea"},{"examples":[{"text":"Dentists would always instruct, say aah!","bold_text_offsets":[[36,40]],"type":"example","id":"78356168-df61-48a2-8e6d-e81a9f4b7bfa"}],"glosses":["Indication of mouth being opened wide."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"bbc2ed13-d118-4554-af46-1536290a55da"},{"examples":[{"text":"Aah. Now I understand.","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"debe6259-8a22-4f65-9f43-23484156f494"}],"glosses":["To express understanding."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"565b4f8d-a140-45c3-9f4d-bf0a1570806c"},{"examples":[{"text":"AAAHHH! A bug! A bug! Get it off me! Get it off me!","bold_text_offsets":[[0,6]],"type":"example","id":"a729dbf3-2b4f-48e9-85d6-ccd24d3b7751"},{"text":"Aah! A rat!","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"1baa2a3b-b34d-42ba-8463-ef9a912f76f4"}],"glosses":["The sound of one screaming (with as many a's or h's as needed for emphasis)."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"00fdffed-3cd2-41cb-8439-fd979a1dc65f"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]}}
